#: angular/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A standalone Angular app (via Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular`, no "
"Angular CLI) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"and\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(pantoken custom elements\n"
"for Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` calls `registerPantokenElements()` (from `@pantoken/"
"angular`) once at bootstrap so\n"
"  elements like `<instui-icon>` work in templates, and imports the token/"
"component CSS plus\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, and other component "
"behaviors out of the\n"
"  box).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` is a standalone component (`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` "
"lets the template\n"
"  compiler accept pantoken's custom element tags) whose template is styled "
"with `instui-*`\n"
"  classes; optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"are marked with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En fristående Angular-app (via Vite + `@analogjs/vite-plugin-angular`, ingen "
"Angular CLI) stylad med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/components) "
"och\n"
"[`@pantoken/angular`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/angular) "
"(pantoken-anpassade element\n"
"för Angular).\n"
"\n"
"## Utveckla\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Vad som finns här\n"
"\n"
"- `src/main.ts` anropar `registerPantokenElements()` (från `@pantoken/"
"angular`) en gång vid bootstrap så\n"
"  att element som `<instui-icon>` fungerar i mallar, och importerar token-/"
"komponent-CSS samt\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (kopplar upp modal-, tooltip- och andra "
"komponentbeteenden direkt).\n"
"- `src/app.component.ts` är en fristående komponent "
"(`CUSTOM_ELEMENTS_SCHEMA` låter mallkompilatorn\n"
"  acceptera pantokens anpassade elementtaggar) vars mall är stylad med "
"`instui-*`\n"
"  klasser; valfria insättningspunkter (header, filters, content, trailing) "
"markeras med\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"- Applicera klasser som `class=\"instui-button\"` på markup; se\n"
"  [komponentreferensen](https://pantoken.app/api/css) för hela klasslistan.\n"
"\n"
"## Lär dig mer\n"
"\n"
"Se [kom igång-guiden](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) för att "
"lära dig mer.\n"

#: canvas-theme-editor/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Upload-ready assets for Canvas LMS's **Theme Editor**, plus a local preview "
"for authoring Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) page templates styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — upload these two files under **Theme Editor → "
"Advanced** in Canvas.\n"
"  They're built for the CDN provider/theme/mode you chose when scaffolding "
"(`--cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light by default) and include a loader "
"for\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up component behaviors like modal, "
"tooltip, and drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — a local, TinyMCE-based editor (`npm run "
"dev`) that mirrors Canvas's\n"
"  RCE so you can author page templates against pantoken's classes before "
"copying them into Canvas.\n"
"  The page itself is built with pantoken's `wrapper` layout: click **Edit "
"theme** to open a tray\n"
"  with **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** tabs (CDN provider/theme/mode selects, "
"and syntax-highlighted,\n"
"  hand-editable copies of `theme.css`/`theme.js` that feed the live "
"preview), and the **?** button\n"
"  for full instructions. Use the **Layouts** toolbar button to start from "
"one of pantoken's bundled\n"
"  starter page layouts (hero, callout, two-column, rubric note, "
"testimonial), sourced from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"This opens a Vite dev server with:\n"
"\n"
"- An **editor** pane (TinyMCE, matching the version/config\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) itself "
"uses — see below).\n"
"  Use the **Layouts** button to load one of the bundled starter layouts "
"(this replaces the whole\n"
"  document, after a confirm, rather than inserting at the cursor), and the "
"**Source code** toggle\n"
"  to hand-edit the raw HTML in a syntax-highlighted (CodeMirror) view "
"alongside the editor, with\n"
"  the preview pane updating live as you type — unlike TinyMCE's stock `code` "
"plugin, which edits in\n"
"  a one-shot modal dialog with no live preview.\n"
"- A **preview** pane showing the editor's content with the current CSS/JS "
"tab's stylesheet/script\n"
"  applied (not just the resolved CDN URLs), wrapped to match Canvas's own "
"content-area background\n"
"  and max width — a faithful \"what this will look like once uploaded to "
"Canvas\" check, updated\n"
"  live as you type or edit the theme.\n"
"- The editor and preview panes sit in a split view you can resize by "
"dragging the divider, stack\n"
"  vertically instead of side by side, and swap the order of (drag a pane's "
"toolbar onto the other,\n"
"  or use the **Swap panes** button). Each pane has its own fullscreen "
"button.\n"
"- The **Edit theme** tray's **Config** tab holds the CDN provider/theme/mode "
"selects and\n"
"  **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js** links; its **CSS**/**JS** "
"tabs are editable copies\n"
"  of the generated files — hand-edit them and the preview picks up your "
"changes directly. Changing\n"
"  a Config select re-generates the CSS/JS tabs unless you've already edited "
"them, in which case a\n"
"  **Regenerate from config** button appears instead of silently overwriting "
"your edit.\n"
"\n"
"## Workflow\n"
"\n"
"1. Upload `theme.css` and `theme.js` to Canvas's Theme Editor (**Advanced → "
"CSS / JavaScript**) so\n"
"   pantoken's classes are available on every page.\n"
"2. Run `npm run dev`, use **Layouts** to start from a bundled starter, and "
"edit it like you\n"
"   would in Canvas's own RCE.\n"
"3. Click **Copy HTML** and paste the result into a Canvas page's RCE (switch "
"to the HTML editor\n"
"   view first). Canvas sanitizes pasted HTML server-side — this scaffold "
"doesn't attempt to\n"
"   replicate that, so always verify the pasted result in Canvas (see \"Notes "
"on Canvas's RCE\"\n"
"   below).\n"
"\n"
"## Notes on Canvas's RCE\n"
"\n"
"The Canvas Rich Content Editor runs TinyMCE and sanitizes submitted HTML on "
"the server against an\n"
"allowlist (`gems/canvas_sanitize` in canvas-lms, kept in sync with TinyMCE's "
"own\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). What that allowlist means for "
"templates built here:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, and `aria-*` attributes are "
"allowed on every element —\n"
"  pantoken's `class=\"instui-*\"` styling hooks (and inline `style`, e.g. "
"for CSS anchor positioning)\n"
"  **do** survive being pasted and saved, contrary to older guidance in this "
"file. `<script>` tags\n"
"  are always stripped.\n"
"- **RCE-safe pantoken components**: static/display components — alert, view, "
"heading, text, table,\n"
"  a button-as-`<a>` (not a real `<button>`), blockquote. Stick to semantic "
"HTML pantoken already\n"
"  supports (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, headings, lists, tables).\n"
"- **RCE-unsafe**: anything from `@pantoken/interactions`'s behavior set — "
"modal, tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, or any other component driven by the native "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributes. Those attributes aren't in Canvas's "
"sanitizer allowlist, so\n"
"  the markup survives but the interactive behavior silently breaks the first "
"time the page is\n"
"  saved in Canvas, even with `theme.js`'s `@pantoken/interactions` loader "
"present. Real form\n"
"  elements (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) and "
"inline `<svg>` are\n"
"  stripped outright — none of the bundled starter templates use them.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` loads `@pantoken/interactions` from the CDN, which runs in "
"Canvas's global page scope —\n"
"useful for interactions on pages you build directly in Canvas's RCE with raw "
"HTML edits, but (per\n"
"above) any `popover`/`command`-attribute-driven markup pasted from the RCE "
"preview here won't stay\n"
"interactive once saved.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"Uppladdningsklara tillgångar för Canvas LMS:s **Theme Editor**, plus en "
"lokal förhandsvisning för att skapa Rich\n"
"Content Editor (RCE) sidmallar stylade med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components).\n"
"\n"
"## Vad som finns här\n"
"\n"
"- `theme.css` / `theme.js` — ladda upp dessa två filer under **Theme Editor "
"→ Advanced** i Canvas.\n"
"  De är byggda för den CDN-leverantör/tema/läge du valde vid scaffolding (`--"
"cdn`/`--theme`/\n"
"  `--theme-mode`; jsDelivr/rebrand/light som standard) och inkluderar en "
"loader för\n"
"  `@pantoken/interactions` (kopplar upp komponentbeteenden som modal, "
"tooltip och drilldown).\n"
"- `index.html` / `src/main.ts` — en lokal TinyMCE-baserad editor (`npm run "
"dev`) som speglar Canvas's\n"
"  RCE så att du kan skapa sidmallar mot pantoken:s klasser innan du kopierar "
"dem till Canvas.\n"
"  Sidan är byggd med pantoken:s `wrapper` layout: klicka **Edit theme** för "
"att öppna en panel\n"
"  med **Config** / **CSS** / **JS** flikar (CDN-leverantör/tema/läge-val "
"samt syntaxmarkerade,\n"
"  handredigerbara kopior av `theme.css`/`theme.js` som matar den live "
"förhandsvisningen), och **?**-knappen\n"
"  för fullständiga instruktioner. Använd verktygsfältknappen **Layouts** för "
"att starta från en av pantoken:s paketbundna\n"
"  startsidlayouter (hero, callout, tvåkolumn, rubric note, testimonial), "
"hämtade från\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts).\n"
"\n"
"## Utveckling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Detta öppnar en Vite dev-server med:\n"
"\n"
"- En **editor**-ruta (TinyMCE, matchande version/konfiguration\n"
"  [instructure/canvas-lms](https://github.com/instructure/canvas-lms) själv "
"använder — se nedan).\n"
"  Använd **Layouts**-knappen för att ladda en av de paketbundna "
"startlayouterna (detta ersätter hela\n"
"  dokumentet, efter bekräftelse, istället för att infoga vid markören), och "
"växeln **Source code**\n"
"  för att handredigera rå HTML i en syntaxmarkerad (CodeMirror) vy bredvid "
"editorn, med\n"
"  förhandsvisningsrutan som uppdateras live medan du skriver — till skillnad "
"från TinyMCE:s standard `code`-plugin, som redigerar i\n"
"  en engångs modal-dialog utan liveförhandsvisning.\n"
"- En **preview**-ruta som visar editorinnehållet med den aktuella CSS/JS-"
"flikens stylesheet/script\n"
"  applicerat (inte bara de uppslagna CDN-URL:erna), inramad för att matcha "
"Canvas:s egen innehållsareas bakgrund\n"
"  och maxbredd — en trogen \"så här kommer det att se ut när det laddats upp "
"till Canvas\"-kontroll, uppdaterad\n"
"  live medan du skriver eller redigerar temat.\n"
"- Editor- och preview-rutorna sitter i en delad vy som du kan ändra storlek "
"på genom att dra skiljelinjen, stapla\n"
"  vertikalt istället för sida vid sida, och byta ordning på dem (dra en ruts "
"verktygsfält över den andra,\n"
"  eller använd knappen **Swap panes**). Varje ruta har sin egen "
"helskärmsknapp.\n"
"- **Edit theme**-panelens **Config**-flik innehåller CDN-leverantör/tema/"
"läge-valen och\n"
"  länkarna **Download theme.css** / **Download theme.js**; dess **CSS**/"
"**JS**-flikar är redigerbara kopior\n"
"  av de genererade filerna — handredigera dem och förhandsvisningen plockar "
"upp dina ändringar direkt. Att ändra\n"
"  ett Config-val återgenererar CSS/JS-flikarna om du inte redan redigerat "
"dem; i så fall visas en\n"
"  **Regenerate from config**-knapp istället för att tyst skriva över din "
"redigering.\n"
"\n"
"## Arbetsflöde\n"
"\n"
"1. Ladda upp `theme.css` och `theme.js` till Canvas Theme Editor (**Advanced "
"→ CSS / JavaScript**) så att\n"
"   pantoken:s klasser finns tillgängliga på varje sida.\n"
"2. Kör `npm run dev`, använd **Layouts** för att börja från en paketbunden "
"start och redigera den som du\n"
"   skulle i Canvas:s egen RCE.\n"
"3. Klicka **Copy HTML** och klistra in resultatet i en Canvas-sidas RCE (byt "
"först till HTML-redigeraren).\n"
"   Canvas sanerar inklistrad HTML på serversidan — detta scaffold försöker "
"inte replikera det, så verifiera alltid\n"
"   det inklistrade resultatet i Canvas (se \"Notes on Canvas's RCE\" "
"nedan).\n"
"\n"
"## Anteckningar om Canvas's RCE\n"
"\n"
"Canvas Rich Content Editor kör TinyMCE och sanerar skickad HTML på servern "
"mot en\n"
"allowlist (`gems/canvas_sanitize` i canvas-lms, hålls synkad med TinyMCE:s "
"egna\n"
"`valid_elements`/`extended_valid_elements`). Vad den allowlisten betyder för "
"mallar byggda här:\n"
"\n"
"- `class`, `id`, `style`, `title`, `role`, och `aria-*` attribut är tillåtna "
"på alla element —\n"
"  pantoken:s `class=\"instui-*\"` stylingkrokar (och inline `style`, t.ex. "
"för CSS-ankarpositionering)\n"
"  **överlever** att klistras in och sparas, till skillnad från äldre råd i "
"denna fil. `<script>` taggar\n"
"  tas alltid bort.\n"
"- **RCE-säkra pantoken-komponenter**: statiska/visningskomponenter — alert, "
"view, heading, text, table,\n"
"  en knapp-som-`<a>` (inte en riktig `<button>`), blockquote. Håll dig till "
"semantisk HTML som pantoken redan\n"
"  stöder (`div`, `p`, `span`, `a`, `img`, rubriker, listor, tabeller).\n"
"- **RCE-osäkra**: allt från `@pantoken/interactions`'s beteendeset — modal, "
"tooltip,\n"
"  drilldown, close-button, eller någon annan komponent driven av de inbyggda "
"`popover`/`popovertarget`/\n"
"  `command`/`commandfor` attributen. Dessa attribut finns inte i Canvas:s "
"sanitizer-allowlist, så\n"
"  markupen överlever men det interaktiva beteendet tyst bryts första gången "
"sidan\n"
"  sparas i Canvas, även med `theme.js`'s `@pantoken/interactions` loader "
"närvarande. Riktiga formulärelement\n"
"  (`input`, `form`, `button`, `select`, `textarea`, `label`) och inline "
"`<svg>` tas\n"
"  bort helt — inga av de paketbundna startmallarna använder dem.\n"
"\n"
"`theme.js` laddar `@pantoken/interactions` från CDN:en, vilket körs i "
"Canvas:s globala sidomfång —\n"
"användbart för interaktioner på sidor du bygger direkt i Canvas's RCE med "
"råa HTML-ändringar, men (enligt\n"
"ovan) kommer någon `popover`/`command`-attributstyrd markup som klistras "
"från RCE-förhandsvisningen här inte förbli\n"
"interaktiv när den väl sparats.\n"

#: components/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A plain TypeScript app (via Vite) styled with\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructure's\n"
"design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` holds the actual page markup — a `wrapper`-layout shell from\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). View source\n"
"  and edit it directly; nothing is injected by JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` imports `@pantoken/css` (defines every `--instui-*` custom "
"property),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (document defaults + focus ring), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*` classes), `@pantoken/interactions` (wires up modal, tooltip, "
"and other component\n"
"  behaviors out of the box), and your own `src/style.css` — add interactive "
"behavior here.\n"
"- Optional insertion points (header, filters, content, trailing) are marked "
"with\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` in `index.html` — replace their contents with "
"your own markup.\n"
"- Apply classes like `class=\"instui-button\"` to markup; see the\n"
"  [component reference](https://pantoken.app/api/css) for the full class "
"list.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [HTML guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En enkel TypeScript-app (via Vite) stylad med\n"
"[`@pantoken/components`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"components), Instructures\n"
"design tokens och ikoner.\n"
"\n"
"## Utveckla\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Vad som finns här\n"
"\n"
"- `index.html` innehåller den faktiska sidans markup — en `wrapper`-"
"layoutskalet från\n"
"  [`@pantoken/plugin-layouts`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/"
"plugin-layouts). Visa källkoden\n"
"  och redigera den direkt; inget injiceras av JavaScript.\n"
"- `src/main.ts` importerar `@pantoken/css` (definierar varje `--instui-*` "
"custom property),\n"
"  `@pantoken/components/base.css` (dokumentstandarder + fokusring), "
"`components.css`\n"
"  (`.instui-*`-klasser), `@pantoken/interactions` (kopplar upp modal, "
"tooltip och andra komponent-\n"
"  beteenden direkt), och din egen `src/style.css` — lägg till interaktivt "
"beteende här.\n"
"- Valfria insättningspunkter (header, filters, content, trailing) är "
"markerade med\n"
"  `<div data-slot=\"...\">` i `index.html` — ersätt deras innehåll med din "
"egen markup.\n"
"- Applicera klasser som `class=\"instui-button\"` på markup; se\n"
"  [komponentreferensen](https://pantoken.app/api/css) för fullständig "
"klasslista.\n"
"\n"
"## Läs mer\n"
"\n"
"Se [HTML-guiden](https://pantoken.app/guide/components) för att lära dig "
"mer.\n"

#: next/README.md
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"A Next.js (App Router) app styled with [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"Instructure's design tokens and icons.\n"
"\n"
"## Develop\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## What's here\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` wraps the config with `withPantoken(...)` (adds pantoken "
"to\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` imports `@pantoken/css`, which defines every `--instui-*` "
"custom\n"
"  property, at the root so it's available on every page, plus the `wrapper` "
"layout's root class on\n"
"  `<body>` and `PantokenInteractions` (a client component that loads "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  wires up modal, tooltip, and other component behaviors out of the box).\n"
"- `app/page.tsx` renders markup styled with `instui-*` classes; optional "
"insertion points (header,\n"
"  filters, content, trailing) are marked with `<div data-slot=\"...\">`.\n"
"\n"
"## Learn more\n"
"\n"
"See the [getting started guide](https://pantoken.app/guide/getting-started) "
"to learn more.\n"
msgstr ""
"# {{projectName}}\n"
"\n"
"En Next.js (App Router) -app stylad med [`@pantoken/next`](https://"
"www.npmjs.com/package/@pantoken/next),\n"
"Instructures designtokens och ikoner.\n"
"\n"
"## Utveckling\n"
"\n"
"```sh\n"
"npm install\n"
"npm run dev\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Vad som finns här\n"
"\n"
"- `next.config.mjs` wrappor konfigurationen med `withPantoken(...)` (lägger "
"till pantoken till\n"
"  `transpilePackages`).\n"
"- `app/layout.tsx` importerar `@pantoken/css`, som definierar varje `--"
"instui-*` anpassad\n"
"  egenskap, i roten så att den är tillgänglig på varje sida, plus `wrapper` "
"layoutens root-klass på\n"
"  `<body>` och `PantokenInteractions` (en klientkomponent som laddar "
"`@pantoken/interactions` —\n"
"  kopplar upp modal, tooltip och andra komponentbeteenden direkt).\n"
